{
  "_comment": "No Lab Required syntax theme. Spec B5: highlighting must use weight or italic in addition to hue, so it still reads on a black-and-white printer. That claim used to be false -- String and Variable were both upright and unbolded and differed only in hue, so they printed identically -- and the palette was a separate design system from the book's, built around a teal that appears on no other page. Three treatments now: bold for the language's own words, italic for text the language does not read as code, plain for everything else.",
